e":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":92,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All five deliverables are in `work/`, along with the analysis scripts. No simulator was run and nothing was fitted.\n\n**Policy:** after the 12 s minimum green, the network almost always switches. It goes to the phase with the strongest demand score: waiting vehicles at the stop lines (a halted car counts 1, a moving one ½), plus a handicap that depends on the current phase. EW_through is the default. In light traffic it holds EW_through even with up to 2 NS-through cars, one west left-turner or one south left-turner waiting. Once arrivals stop, that hold can strand those cars until the simulation cap. In one of six recorded episodes, 3 cars waited about 30 minutes, adding roughly 1.5 veh-h. It ignores queues on the north/south upstream lanes and how long anyone has waited.\n\n**Rule files on the recorded states (minimum green elapsed):**\n\n| file | fidelity | comparisons (counter) | plus uncounted argmax |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `rules_small.py` | 92.08 % | 8 | 3 |\n| `rules_full.py` | 92.19 % | 1 | 6 (one 3-way argmax per decision) |\n\nBoth reach about 90.6 % on the network's own episodes once the stall states are excluded. `rules_full` matches the network better in light traffic and stall situations (91 % vs 87 % on synthetic light-traffic states).\n\n**Predictions:** fidelity 0.90 (small) and 0.905 (full); mean TTS 45.3 and 45.0 veh-h, against the network's 44.7 on the dev episodes.","ttft_ms":1118,"type":"result","duration_ms":1738972,"uuid":"d7019391-d32b-4ec6-a7ea-65534e058f33","ttft_stream_ms":934,"time_to_request_ms":52,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"req